  {
    "Ammunition Name": "Bolt, Angling",
    "Ammunition Type": "Quarrel",
    "Weapon": "Crossbow of Angling",
    "Quantity": "1",
    "Damage Modifier": "+2",
    "Range Modifier": "+0",
    "Cost": "-",
    "Weight": "-",
    "Notes": "PHBR2 p.107. NOT PURCHASABLE and not carried: this bolt is CREATED BY THE CROSSBOW OF ANGLING on command, up to three times per day. It exists as a record because the +2 belongs to the BOLT, not to the bow -- the crossbow itself is an ordinary light crossbow and carries no bonus. Counts as a +2 bolt for attack rolls and damage where applicable. When fired it trails a pencil-thin snaking line of faint blue light (which radiates magic fairly strongly) connecting it to the crossbow. On impact the head expands into a small claw which embeds itself in the target so the bolt grips strongly; a second command word 'reels in' the target, the cord shrinking to drag it to the archer at up to 60 feet per round depending on weight and friction. If the target is heavier than the archer, or immovable or braced, THE CROSSBOWMAN MAY BE DRAGGED TO THE TARGET instead -- which can be exploited to pull oneself up to a ceiling or a wall. The magical cord is AC -2 and takes 15 points of damage to destroy; nonmagical weapons do it no damage."
  },
